  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN260.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">iravukkuṟikkaṇ talaimakaṉ ciṟaippuṟamākat tōḻiyāṟ colleṭukkappaṭṭut talaimakaḷ colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said after the words had been brought up by the confidante while HE was behind the hedge during a night tryst.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN260.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>maṇṭila maḻuka malainiṟaṅ kiḷara</l>
        <l>vaṇṭiṉa malarpāyn tūta micaiya</l>
        <l>kaṇ<supplied>ṭaṟ</supplied> kāṉaṟ kurukiṉa molippat</l>
        <l><anchor n="2"/>tiraipā ṭaviyat timiṟoḻiṉ maṟappat</l>
        <l>takaiyā ṭalava ṉaḷaivayiṟ ceṟiyac</l>
        <l>cekkart tōṉṟat tuṇaipuṇa raṉṟi</l>
        <l>lekkarp peṇṇai yakamaṭal cērak</l>
        <l>kaḻimalar kamaḻmukaṅ karappap poḻiṉmaṉaip</l>
        <l>puṉṉai naṟu<supplied>vī</supplied> poṉṉiṟaṅ koḷā<supplied>a</supplied></l>
        <l>vellai paipayak kaḻippi yelluṟa</l>
        <l>yāṅkā kuvaḷko ṟāṉē nīṅkātu</l>
        <l>mutumarat tuṟaiyu muravuvāy mutupuṭ</l>
        <l>katumeṉak kuḻaṟuṅ kaḻutuvaḻaṅ karainā</l>
        <l>ṇeñcunekiḻ paruvaral ceyta</l>
        <l>vaṉpi lāḷa ṉaṟivunayan tēṉē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">While the [sun-]disk dims, while the mountains shine with colour,</l>
        <l corresp="2">while swarms of bees spread on the blossoms [and] fill themselves, on the height,</l>
        <l corresp="3">while flocks of herons sound in the seashore grove of mangroves,</l>
        <l corresp="4">while the waves cease to sing, while the boats forget [their] task,</l>
        <l corresp="5">while crabs that play as is fit are packed tight in [their] holes,</l>
        <l corresp="6">while the Aṉṟil, uniting with [its] mate, when the redness [of dusk] appears,</l>
        <l corresp="7">joins the inner stems of the Palmyra trees in the dunes,</l>
        <l corresp="8a-c">while the blossoms in the backwaters hide [their] fragrant openings,</l>
        <l corresp="10">while night falls, the daylight being gently spent,</l>
        <l corresp="9">taking the gold colour of the fragrant Puṉṉai blossoms</l>
        <l corresp="8d 11a-c">by the house with [its] grove, what will become of her?</l>
        <l corresp="15">I have been longing for knowledge of the man without love,</l>
        <l corresp="14">who made [her] suffer so that my heart becomes soft,</l>
        <l>at midnight when demons roam, when the old bird with broken beak</l>
        <l corresp="11d-13">that stays in the old tree without leaving, shrieks in quick succession.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

